0</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9"><label>9</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schnabel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Reinhold-Keller</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Willmann</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Gross</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Tolerability of methotrexate starting with 15 or 25 mg/week for rheumatoid arthritis.</article-title><source>Rheumatol Int</source><year>1994</year>;<volume>14</volume>:<fpage>33</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7939138</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10"><label>10</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Verstappen</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>van der Veen</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Heurkens</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Schenk</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ter Borg</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Intensive treatment with methotrexate in early rheumatoid arthritis: aiming for remission. Computer Assisted Management in Early Rheumatoid Arthritis (CAMERA, an open-label strategy trial).</article-title><source>Ann Rheum Dis</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>66</volume>:<fpage>1443</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17519278</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11"><label>11</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lambert</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Sandhu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lochhead</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurst</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name><name><surname>McRorie</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Dhillon</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Dose escalation of parenteral methotrexate in active rheumatoid arthritis that has been unresponsive to conventional doses of methotrexate: a randomized, controlled trial.</article-title><source>Arthritis Rheum</source><year>2004</year>;<volume>50</volume>:<fpage>364</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14872477</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Braun</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaestner</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Flaxenberg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Waehrisch</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanke</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Demary</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group> <article-title>Comparison of the clinical efficacy and safety of subcutaneous versus oral administration of methotrexate in patients with active rheumatoid arthritis.</article-title><source>Arthritis Rheum</source><year>2008</year>;<volume>58</volume>:<fpage>73</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>81</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18163521</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gallagher</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>TY</given-names></name><name><surname>Wyer</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>How to find evidence when you need it, part 3: A clinician&#x02019;s guide to MEDLINE: tricks and special skills.</article-title><source>Ann Emerg Med</source><year>2002</year>;<volume>39</volume>:<fpage>547</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11973563</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glanville</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lefebvre</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Miles</surname><given-names>JN</given-names></name><name><surname>Camosso-Stefinovic</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>How to identify randomized controlled trials in MEDLINE: ten years on.</article-title><source>J Med Libr Assoc</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>94</volume>:<fpage>130</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16636704</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Oxford Centre for Evidence-based Medicine</collab> <source>Levels of evidence</source>. <comment><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cebm.net/index.aspx?o=1025">http://www.cebm.net/index.aspx?o&#x0200a;=&#x0200a;1025</ext-link> (accessed March 2008)</comment></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kazis</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Meenan</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name></person-group> <article-title>Effect sizes for interpreting changes in health-status.</article-title><source>Medical Care</source><year>1989</year>;<volume>27</volume><issue>(3 suppl)</issue>:<fpage>S178</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>89</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2646488</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen</surname><giv